    {
      "id": "0qx28qm",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "RRB HIGH-VALUE EXAM POINTS"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "px7v9tz",
      "content": "• Exchange rate determined by demand &amp; supply in flexible system.<br></br>• Depreciation boosts exports but increases import cost.<br></br>• USA is major export partner; China major import source.<br></br>• Crude oil is India’s largest import item."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "drfursb",
      "content": "• BoP consists of Current and Capital Accounts.<br></br>• CAD occurs when imports exceed exports.<br></br>• India follows managed floating exchange rate.<br></br>• Depreciation increases export competitiveness.<br></br>• Forex reserves maintained by RBI.<br></br>"
    }
  ],
